# Vulnerabilities accepted, with the reason and a date to revisit.
#
# Nothing goes in here to make a build green. Each entry must name why the
# finding cannot currently be fixed, and carry an expiry so it comes back.

# cryptography 49.0.0 — HIGH, fixed upstream in 50.0.0.
#
# Not fixable from this repository today: mlflow requires `cryptography<50`, and
# mlflow itself is pinned to >=3.15.0 because older releases carry 17 CVEs, seven
# of them CRITICAL (arbitrary command execution, path traversal, credential
# exfiltration, unauthenticated SSRF). Forcing cryptography>=50 makes the
# dependency set unresolvable — pip refuses the install outright.
#
# Exposure here is limited: cryptography arrives transitively through mlflow's
# tracking client, this project never calls it directly, and mlflow is disabled
# in serving (CHURN_MLFLOW_ENABLED=0) and unreachable from the request path.
#
# The same finding is suppressed for pip-audit in .github/workflows/ci.yml under
# its identifier PYSEC-2026-3552. The two scanners use different IDs; keep them in
# step.
#
# Revisit when mlflow relaxes its upper bound. Remove BOTH entries then — do not
# extend the expiry without re-checking.
CVE-2026-69247 exp:2026-12-31

# AWS-0104 — security group allows egress to any IP address.
#
# The deployment is a single instance in a public subnet that installs packages
# from Ubuntu and Docker mirrors and reaches ECR, S3, SSM and CloudWatch. Those
# are AWS service ranges plus third-party mirrors whose addresses change, so
# pinning destination CIDRs would break the node on a routine upstream change
# rather than protect it.
#
# What has been done instead: egress is restricted to 443/tcp, 80/tcp and 53/udp,
# so there is no arbitrary outbound channel on other ports.
#
# Eliminating internet egress means VPC endpoints for S3, ECR, SSM and
# CloudWatch. The S3 gateway endpoint is free; the interface endpoints are about
# $7/month each — a large fraction of a ~$18/month deployment. Revisit if this
# grows past a single node, at which point the endpoint cost is proportionally
# small.
AVD-AWS-0104 exp:2026-12-31
